  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-235959",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "We find the ranges of the individual pieces, and then calculate their union:\n\n- The range of the branch defined on $x\\in [-3,0)$ is $[0,2)$\n\n- The range of the branch defined on $x\\in [0,3]$ is $[-3,-1]$\n\nTherefore, the range of $f(x)$ is $[-3,-1]\\cup [0,2).$\n\n**Note:** From the graph, we see that the value $y=2$ is NOT a valid output of the function $y=f(x).$ Therefore, we use parentheses $(…)$ instead of brackets $[…]$ at this endpoint.",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
